# Hooks deliberately not registered in the template .claude/settings.json.
# Format: one file name per line; everything after # is the reason.
# Checked by: scripts/check-orphan-hooks.sh (issue #310, #323).
#
# The list is not a place where defects become invisible. Each line must
# name the reason and the next step. An empty reason = a defect, not an exception.
#
# Libraries and CLIs located next to the hooks (rule-engine.sh, residency-gate-*.sh,
# agent-trace-uploader.sh) are NOT added to this list: they carry the marker
# `# claude-hook: false — …` in the header, and the watchdog recognizes it itself (2026-08-04,
# peer session on issues #310/#321/#323).
#
agent-trace-recorder.sh     # local telemetry (tool traces in the home directory): enabled by the user's deliberate opt-in, the retention contract is not defined — off by default in the template. To enable: add to settings.json Stop+PostToolUse.
pack-creator-spf-guard.sh   # the hook works, but there is no activation contract: nobody sets PACK_CREATOR_ACTIVE=1 in the template runtime (a skill cannot pass env to the hook process). Next step: activation via a state file from the pack-creator skill + 3 tests (normal session / active deny / active allow).
